Description: antinomie: debug engine: Debug on start and the auxiliary vector
Author: MikiMiku <jonathanirvinjo@gmail.com>
Origin: project
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-20

EXEC takes a new flag, DEBUG: the new program stops before its first user instruction. The launch creates the debug session for the task that is about to exec; a task_work callback added before the exec runs at the first return to user mode (the loader's entry for a dynamic program, the ELF entry for a static one, whatever the address space layout) and parks the task. ATTACH then adopts the session by identity, and the reply of EXEC carries the start time that identity needs. The session learns its address space at that first park; nothing in the group runs, reads or writes memory before it. Detaching lets the program run.  AUXV returns the auxiliary vector the kernel gave the program at exec, which is how a debugger places a position independent program and its loader.  CAPS gains START and AUXV. Contract revision stays 17.

